    "description": "Let `C` be a chain complex of free `\u2124`-modules and `G` an abelian group. Then for every `n` there\nis a short exact sequence\n`0 \u2192 H\u2099(C) \u2297 G \u2192 H\u2099(C \u2297 G) \u2192 Tor\u2081(H\u2099\u208b\u2081(C), G) \u2192 0`,\nnatural in `C` and `G`, and split (non-naturally).\n\n*Status.* We proved the theorem for the two-term free complex `C = (\u2124 --(\u00b7k)--> \u2124)` in both\ndegrees: `H\u2080(G \u2297 C) \u2245 G \u2297 H\u2080(C)` (`uctHomologyZeroIso`, no correction term since `H\u208b\u2081 = 0`) and\n`H\u2081(G \u2297 C) \u2245 Tor\u2081(G, H\u2080(C))` (`uctHomologyOneIso`, pure correction term since `H\u2081(C) = 0`,\n`isZero_resComplex_homology_one`); the correction term is genuinely nonzero\n(`not_isZero_uct_tor_term`, `torOneZMod_self_ne_zero`). We also proved the flat-coefficient case\n`H\u2099(C \u2297 G) \u2245 H\u2099(C) \u2297 G` for arbitrary complexes over any commutative ring\n(`homologyTensorFlatIso`). Proving the general statement needs freeness of submodules of free\n`\u2124`-modules (cf. C2) and the splitting `C \u2245 Z \u2295 B[-1]`. Falsified by a free complex `C`, a group\n`G` and a degree `n` where the displayed sequence is not exact.",
