    "consumed_by_exp_id": "",
    "description": "The exact-relation half is now proved.  With a node of hypotenuse `c` drawn at radius\n`r = 1 \u2212 1/c`, `drawn_curve_equation` gives the closed relation\n`\u2016dir v \u2212 dir p\u2016\u00b2 = 2 d (1 \u2212 r)/c_p` between the angular and the radial coordinate along\nthe spoke of charge `d`, and `draw_tendsto_dir` shows the drawn curve really does run into\nthe boundary star centre.  The remaining, geometric half is:\n\n  the drawn image of a spoke is, up to a bi-Lipschitz reparametrisation, a genuine\n  Euclidean horocycle of the Poincar\u00e9 disc with curvature a function of `d/c_p` alone, and\n  no drawn spoke is an arc of a circle orthogonal to the boundary (no spoke is a geodesic).\n\n*The key insight is* that the proved relation `\u2016dir v \u2212 dir p\u2016\u00b2 = 2 d (1 \u2212 r)/c_p` is\n*exactly* the equation of a Euclidean circle internally tangent to the unit circle at\n`dir p`, once the drawn radius `r` is converted to the Poincar\u00e9 radial coordinate; so the\nconjecture is the statement that this coordinate change is bi-Lipschitz on `r \u2208 [0,1)`,\nwhich is a one-variable estimate on `1 \u2212 1/c` versus `tanh`.\n\n*Why now?* All the arithmetic input is proved: `drawn_curve_equation` supplies the exact\nalgebraic relation, `contact_order_two_lower` / `contact_order_two_upper` pin the contact\norder at two, which already rules out first-order-contact radii, and `chord_sq_ratio`\nseparates spokes of different charge quantitatively.\n\n---",
