    "description": "**Conjecture.** If `A` and `B` are weight-graded dg-algebras that are `wt`-pure, then the graded\ntensor product `A \u2297 B` (bigraded by the sum of bidegrees) is `wt`-pure, hence formal; and purity\npasses to filtered colimits of weight-graded dg-algebras with weight-preserving transition maps.\nConsequently formality for spaces satisfying weight-monodromy is stable under products and under\npassage to limits of admissible covers.\n\n*The key insight is* that purity is a *pointwise* condition on bidegrees and the diagonal\n`w = wt n` is a subgroup of `\u2124\u00b2`, so it is preserved by every operation that adds bidegrees.\n\n*Why now?* The definitions in this development are already stated bidegree-wise, and the\nK\u00fcnneth-type step needed is exactly the statement that the diagonal is closed under addition,\nwhich is used (and proved) in `sPiece_mul_le`. Falsifiable: a pure `A` and pure `B` whose\ntensor product has cohomology off the diagonal.",
