    "description": "**Status of the base case.** The *qualitative* nonabelian statement was proved in\nthis cycle: `Nonabelian.nonabelian_discrete_poincare` shows that for any group\n`G`, a transition cochain on a connected nerve comes from a global relabelling\niff its monodromy around every closed walk is trivial, and\n`perm_monodromy_obstructs_global_labelling` (with the realised example\n`exTransition_no_global_labelling`) gives the `k`-class instance.\n\n**Statement (open).** For a `k`-class classifier with continuous score vector\n`s : E \u2192 \u211d^k` and a cover with overlap scale `\u03b4`, the following are equivalent:\n(i) every region admits a local `L\u221e` certificate of radius `\u03b4` for its argmax\nclass; (ii) the permutation monodromy of the label-transport cochain is trivial\non every loop of the nerve.  Moreover, when the monodromy is nontrivial, the\ncertified radius of some region is at most `\u03b4`, witnessed by a point where two\nclass scores tie.\n\n**The key insight is** that the binary equivalence proved here\n(`local_certificates_glue_iff_global` together with\n`holonomy_obstructs_uniform_certificate`) is the `k = 2` case of a statement in\nwhich \"sign change\" is replaced by \"argmax change\", and the intermediate value\ntheorem is replaced by a tie-point argument on the difference of two coordinates.\n\n**Why now?** Both halves already exist separately: the nonabelian gluing theorem\nis proved, and the analytic tie-point argument is a two-coordinate instance of\n`exists_boundary_point_near`.\n\n**Falsifier.** A `3`-class cover with trivial monodromy but no global certificate\nat radius `\u03b4` \u2014 e.g. produced by an argmax that changes without any pairwise tie\ninside a region \u2014 would refute the equivalence.",
