    "description": "The proof of `ratConic_pos_empty_of_isSquare_disc` yields more than emptiness.  In the primitive\nsquare-discriminant case, with `a = f\u00b2 - e\u00b2`, `b = e f`, `gcd(e,f) = 1`, the *inhomogeneous* line\n`b m\u00b2 - a m n - b n\u00b2 = c` with `0 < |c| \u2264 b` has all of its solutions with `m, n > 0` bounded by\n\n  `f m + e n \u2264 |c| \u2264 e f`,  hence  `m \u2264 e` and `n \u2264 f`,  hence  `max(m,n) \u2264 b`,\n\nand the only unbounded case is `c = 0`, which is the pair of asymptotes `e m = f n`.  So a\nsquare-discriminant conic degenerates in a completely controlled way: `c = b` is empty, every other\nsmall `c` gives a set of size `O(d(|c|))` inside the box `[1,e] \u00d7 [1,f]`.\n\n**The key insight is** that the factorization `(e m - f n)(f m + e n) = c` bounds the *second*\nfactor by `|c|` as soon as the first is nonzero, and the second factor already dominates both\n`f m` and `e n`.\n\n**Why now?**  The factorization and the parametrization are formalized inside\n`ratConic_primitive_empty` and `factored_conic_no_pos_solution`; only the bookkeeping of a general\nright-hand side `c` remains, together with the `c = 0` degeneration.",
